# Anzrag, the Quake-Mole: "{3}{R}{R}{G}{G}: Anzrag must be blocked each combat this turn if able" (CR 509.1c, 611.2c). Turn 1: four
# of Bot1's five Moxes cast Anzrag, and an Ornithopter costs {0}. Turn 2: Bot2 casts two Ornithopters. Turn 5: Bot1 pays
# {3}{R}{R}{G}{G} with the five Moxes and two Forests, then attacks with Anzrag and its Ornithopter. Bot2 may not declare no
# block, nor block only the Ornithopter: it blocks Anzrag with its Ornithopter#1. The trigger gives an additional combat phase, and the
# requirement is still there in it ("each combat this turn"): Bot2 may not decline to block again, Ornithopter#2 must block
# Anzrag, and dies as well; the third combat phase has no blocker left and Anzrag deals 8 to Bot2. In Bot1's next turn the
# ability is gone (CR 514.2): Bot2 declares no block with a third Ornithopter and takes 8 again.

